<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="186" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Send Email dialog: turn on templates and AI drafting (and confirm attachments) in every host (D-219 Q3)</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (UAT round 4)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared client code (.ts/.tsx) used by several wizards.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Wiring two existing handlers into existing hosts, with a reference host that already does it.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, fluent-ui, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>The owner (D-219 Q3) found that the Send Email dialog (the Console Quick Start "Send Email" card and "Send as email" chip, and the file preview's email) shows no template picker and no AI drafting. EmailComposer hides both when the host does not pass `onListEmailTemplates` / `onDraftWithAi`. Pass them.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and the @spaarke/ui-components wizard framework (CreateRecordWizard, WizardShell).</role>
  <goal>Every SendEmailDialog host passes onListEmailTemplates and onDraftWithAi from createXrmEmailComposeHandlers, so the template picker and the AI draft sparkle appear; attachments keep working.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>SpaarkeAi ConversationPane.tsx ~3588-3599 renders SendEmailDialog without the two handlers, though the same file's EmailPerItemCards path already uses createXrmEmailComposeHandlers (EmailPerItemCards.tsx:237-239). LegalWorkspace FilePreview/FilePreviewDialog.tsx:169-180 likewise. Reference: Spaarke.AI.Widgets EmailWorkspaceWidget.tsx:218-220.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/FilePreview/FilePreviewDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/EmailWorkspaceWidget.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner directive 2026-11-12, applies to every file this task touches: reuse the existing side-pane lookup (`DataverseLookupField` over `INavigationService.openLookup`) and the existing `EmailComposer`; never re-create either. A third rendering of the lookup pattern is a defect (review section 4 item 6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Every component changed in this task stays in `@spaarke/ui-components` and receives Dataverse access only through injected services (`INavigationService`, `IDataService`, `authenticatedFetch`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every UI change in this task uses Fluent v9 and semantic tokens only; light and dark both fully themed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner D-219 (2026-11-12, notes/decisions.md) Q3: templates and AI drafting ON in the Send Email dialog.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Grep every SendEmailDialog / SendEmailPane / SendEmailPage host (excluding tests) and wire each one that lacks the handlers; list the hosts and results in task notes. Build the handlers with the host's existing createXrmEmailComposeHandlers instance where one exists; do not create a second.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-ui-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-react-version-boundaries.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/wizard-side-pane-lookup-and-email-compose.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Composer host wiring" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/EmailWorkspaceWidget.tsx">Passes onListEmailTemplates and onDraftWithAi from createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Grep the SendEmailDialog/Pane/Page hosts; record which lack the handlers.</step>
    <step order="2">Pass onListEmailTemplates and onDraftWithAi in each.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a test per changed host asserting the handlers reach the dialog; run the dev check.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="6">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-186-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a host cannot build compose handlers (no Xrm or BFF access), STOP and list it rather than adding a new handler implementation.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Send Email dialog shows templates and AI">
      <steps>
        <step>Console → Quick Start → Send Email</step>
        <step>Open the template picker; apply a template</step>
        <step>Use AI draft</step>
        <step>Attach a file; send to yourself</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Template picker and AI sparkle present; the template fills the body; AI draft fills the body; the attachment arrives; dark mode themed.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-186-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every non-test SendEmailDialog/SendEmailPane/SendEmailPage host passes onListEmailTemplates and onDraftWithAi (list in task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">In the Console Send Email dialog the template picker and the AI draft button render; with the handlers removed they do not (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Attachments still upload and send as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched folders pass; tsc clean; no new ESLint errors in touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes> Source: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md (Fable review 2026-11-12) and UAT round 4 findings F-R4-2 / F-R4-3 (notes/uat-v4-log.md).</notes>
